{
  // Everything that is run but not shipped: the fitting suite under `tests/`, the one-shot
  // migrations under `scripts/`, and their tests.
  //
  // These were invisible. `tsconfig.json` includes only `src`, so `tsc --noEmit` never looked at
  // them while vitest ran them happily — which is how a broken import into `tests/fitting/` got
  // committed and only died at run time. Widening the app's own `include` would have fixed that
  // by making `npm run build` typecheck code that is never built, so the two projects are kept
  // apart and `npm run typecheck` runs both.
  //
  // No `types` entry is needed: all 59 test files import `describe`/`it`/`expect` from `vitest`
  // by name rather than leaning on `globals: true`.
  //
  // `src/vite-env.d.ts` is listed because this project compiles `src` — through the imports of
  // everything under `tests` — without including it, so the ambient declarations `src` relies on
  // have to be named. Without it `import.meta.env` and Vite's `?url` imports are errors here and
  // nowhere else, which reads as a broken file rather than a missing reference.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["tests", "scripts", "src/vite-env.d.ts"]
}
